{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"BLOCKER — the fix needs a file outside this ticket's declared Scope/file_impact.\n\nThe plan was written when 7de4/7761 was NOT on origin/main. It has since landed, bringing\ntests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py, which pins the exact behaviour 48b3 removes. Implementing\nthe plan verbatim (models_at_or_above -> [model]; largest_window_tokens -> ladder minimum, both\nfor a TRUTHY-but-unlocated primary) turns three of its assertions red:\n\n  test_models_at_or_above_returns_todays_bare_ids_with_no_classes_configured\n    models_at_or_above('some-unknown-model') == _TODAY_LADDER  ->  == ['some-unknown-model']\n  test_largest_window_tokens_still_matches_a_provider_qualified_id\n    largest_window_tokens('some-unknown-model') == MODEL_LADDER[-1][1]\n      ->  == min(w for _, w in MODEL_LADDER)\n  test_start_rung_location_for_a_foreign_family_is_unchanged\n    the whole test is the nova pin; both assertions invert.\n\nThe plan ANTICIPATED the third one ('whichever of the two lands SECOND updates that one\nassertion') but could not name the file, so it is absent from Scope and file_impact. The other\ntwo are the same defect expressed through 'some-unknown-model' and were not enumerated.\n\nEverything inside the declared scope is DONE and green: sizing.py fixed, new RED-first\nregression tests in test_plan_review.py and test_plan_review_prerequisites.py all pass, and\nprerequisites.py is unedited (its existing IndexError handler converts the one-element ladder\ninto the input-too-large indeterminate, as the plan predicted). make lint and make typecheck\nboth exit 0.\n\nAlso stale in the plan: it asserts models_at_or_above('bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8-v1:0')\n== ['claude-opus-4-8']. Post-7de4 that returns the primary verbatim (provider-agreement rule).\nThat is 7de4 behaviour on a LOCATED primary, untouched by this change, so the back-compat test\nhere asserts 'anthropic:claude-opus-4-8' -> ['claude-opus-4-8'] instead.\n\nNot closing. Needs a decision on extending scope to tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785698332120011001,"uuid":"3c33c014-7b73-4d18-9b3a-6ec28421bdab"}